==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|lifa|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|libjanan|lang=gem-pro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɪːva/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɪːva|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|lifði|lifað}}

# {{intransitive}} to [[live]]
#* Genesis 5:3 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20bók%20Móse+5:3&version=ICELAND Icelandic], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Fyrsta%20b%C3%B3k%20M%C3%B3se%205:3&version=NIV English])
#*: ''Adam '''lifði''' hundrað og þrjátíu ár. Þá gat hann son í líking sinni, eftir sinni mynd, og nefndi hann Set.''
#*:: When Adam had '''lived''' 130 years, he had a son in his own likeness, in his own image; and he named him Seth.
# {{transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[experience]] something{{jump|is|experience|s}}
# {{ambitransitive|governs the accusative}} to [[survive]], to [[endure]], to [[come through]]{{jump|is|survive|s}}
#: ''Ég '''lifi'''.''
#:: I'll '''come through'''.
# {{intransitive|of fire}} to [[burn]]{{jump|is|burn|s}}
#: ''Eldurinn '''lifir'''.''
#:: The fire is '''burning'''

